# employee/ — the staff orders app. Copy to .env.local for local dev.
#
# Where the API lives. Left empty (the default) requests go to this app's own
# origin, which in dev means Vite's /api proxy (see vite.config.ts) and in
# production means the Fastify service that serves this SPA. Either way the
# session cookie stays same-origin, which is the reason to prefer it.
#
# Set it to the API's origin only if you deliberately want cross-origin dev —
# and then add that origin to the backend's PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGINS, or CORS will
# reject every call.
VITE_API_BASE_URL=

# Backend the dev proxy forwards /api to. Defaults to http://localhost:3000.
# VITE_API_PROXY_TARGET=http://localhost:3000
